# One effect variable instantiated with a row of **two written labels**, which
# is the union half of the pack convention (the knife plan's §2.1, verbatim).
#
# `twice` declares a lone `!e`, so rule 丁 gives it one erased evidence slot and
# the arity is fixed before any call site exists. The call below instantiates
# `!e := !(Ask|Tell)` and has to put *two* answers in that one word: the pack is
# `ev$Pack{key(Ask), ev$Ask, ev$Pack{key(Tell), ev$Tell, <empty>}}`. Two keys,
# one slot -- the shape a positional evidence vector could not have held, since
# the position of a label in the instance has nothing to do with the position of
# the variable in the declaration.
#
# What makes this a *runtime* case rather than a checker one is that the closure
# reads both. `tell(x)` is one lookup and `ask()` is another, and they are the
# first and second nodes of the same chain, so a build that kept one atom and
# dropped the rest is a wrong answer here and green everywhere else in the tree.
# The `tell` arm prints, so a lookup that reached the wrong node or no node at
# all cannot be silent about it.
#
# `pure_slot` is the control inside the file: the same `twice`, the same slot,
# instantiated with nothing. That path is the identity forward -- no node, no
# allocation -- and it is what every effect-polymorphic signature in std takes,
# so it has to keep working while the line above it does not.
use std/io
use std/list

effect Ask {
  fn ask() -> Int
}

effect Tell {
  fn tell(v: Int) -> Unit
}

fn twice[T, U](xs: List[T], f: fn(T) -> U !e) -> List[U] !e = list.map(xs, f)

pub fn main() -> Unit !io = {
  with handle Ask { ask() => 7 }
  with handle Tell { tell(v) => println("tell ${v}") }
  println("-- two labels in one variable's slot, both read --")
  println(to_string(twice([1, 2], x => {
    tell(x)
    x + ask()
  })))
  println("-- the same slot instantiated with nothing, which is the forward --")
  println(to_string(twice([1, 2], x => x + 100)))
  println("-- and with one of the two, which is a single node over the empty --")
  println(to_string(twice([1, 2], x => x + ask())))
}
